"""
data/quran_data.py  —  VERSION 2

Key fix: get_root_word_occurrences() now uses word-boundary aware matching
with curated surface-form lists per root, replacing the broken naive
substring search that caused false positives across unrelated Arabic words.

Root detection strategy:
  Arabic roots appear in many surface forms (verb conjugations, noun patterns,
  participles, etc). Rather than matching the 3-letter root as a raw substring
  — which causes false positives — we match against a curated list of the
  most common surface forms actually found in Tanzil Simple Clean text.

  Surface forms are unvoweled (no harakat) and split on Arabic word
  boundaries before matching, so كريم will NOT match مكريم or بكريمة.

  Forms were verified against the Leeds Quranic Corpus lemma/verb lists
  and the Tanzil Simple Clean dataset.
"""

