# ── Root surface forms ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# FIX: Instead of matching the raw 3-letter root as a substring (which causes
# false positives — رحم matches مرحبا, كريم matches تكريم, etc.), we now match
# against a curated set of actual surface word forms for each root as they
# appear in Tanzil Simple Clean (unvoweled) text.
#
# Matching is word-boundary aware: the text is split on spaces and each token
# is checked against the forms list. Prefixes like و، ف، ب، ل، ال are stripped
# before matching to handle attached particles.
#
# Forms are the most frequent unvoweled surface forms from the Leeds corpus.
# This approach gives high precision. It may miss rare conjugations but
# eliminates false positives which is the worse problem.

